{**
 * c-tabs - several views of one thing, one shown at a time, and a row of tabs
 * to switch between them.
 *
 * **What the server draws is every panel one under another, each under its
 * title**, and that is what somebody gets whose browser did not run the
 * script: all of it, in order, readable. The tabs are assets/tabs.ts's, laid
 * over this markup once the page has loaded - the tab list, the roles, the one
 * tab the Tab key stops on, the arrow keys, Home and End, and the hiding of
 * every panel but one (the pattern of the ARIA Authoring Practices). None of
 * that is written here, because every piece of it would be a claim about a
 * control nothing yet answers: a role="tab" the server wrote is a tab that
 * does nothing until a script arrives, and a panel it hid is content nobody
 * without the script can reach.
 *
 * $panels names the panels, in order: the block of the caller that draws each
 * one => its title. The script names each tab after its panel's title, which
 * is why the title is the first thing in the panel. $label names the tab list
 * and is kept on the root for the script to put there.
 *
 * $level makes the titles headings of that level (2 to 6, see
 * Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\HeadingLevel), so that without the
 * script the panels are parts of the page's outline. Without a level a title
 * is only a line over its panel.
 *
 * $id gives every panel an address, the id and the name of its block joined:
 * an address naming a panel, or anything inside one, shows that panel.
 *
 * Use it with {embed block tabs}, one {block} for each name in $panels.
 *
 * @param array<string, string> $panels the name of the block drawing each panel => its title
 *}

{define tabs, string $label, array $panels, ?string $id = null, ?int $level = null, ?string $testId = null}
    <div class="c-tabs" data-tabs-label="{$label}" data-testid="{$testId}">
        <div n:foreach="$panels as $panel => $title" class="c-tabs__panel" n:attr="id: $id === null ? null : $id . '-' . $panel">
            {if $level === null}
                <p class="c-tabs__title">{$title}</p>
            {else}
                <h2 n:tag="Trilobit\Core\Presentation\Component\HeadingLevel::from($level)->tag()" class="c-tabs__title">{$title}</h2>
            {/if}

            {include block $panel}
        </div>
    </div>
{/define}
